h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 766)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Camera raw, in the box.</b> ARRIRAW, RED R3D and Blackmagic RAW open by dropping them: Asobi names what they are and develops them to a review copy. RED and Blackmagic develop inside Asobi on the GPU and CPU &#8212; nothing to install; ARRI uses ARRI&#8217;s free Reference Tool, which Asobi helps you find; DaVinci Resolve Studio is the fallback for all three.</li>
<li><b>Anamorphic, end to end.</b> View &#9656; Anamorphic Desqueeze now carries through to movie exports: Export Movie, the session reel, and the side-by-side movie and reel write the desqueezed picture, each clip by its own factor, with marks on their features and burn-ins unstretched. Shares to the web stay as recorded.</li>
<li>Marks in a reel now stay on the picture when a clip is letterboxed inside the reel&#8217;s frame. They used to be laid across the whole frame and slide off.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
