        <item>
            <title>0.8</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:19:23 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>751</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 751)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>RED and Blackmagic RAW.</b> Drop <code>.R3D</code> or <code>.braw</code> files and Asobi names them and develops them like ARRIRAW. R3D develops inside Asobi on the GPU &#8212; nothing to install, an 8K clip in a few seconds &#8212; to Log3G10 / REDWideGamutRGB as shot. Blackmagic RAW develops through DaVinci Resolve Studio to ACEScct. Each clip is told which it is, so a mixed card of ARRI, RED and Blackmagic clips is one drop.</li>
<li><b>Compare sizes each side on its own.</b> Side by side shows both pictures at the same height, stacked at the same width, each at its own aspect ratio &#8212; a tall 9:16 beside a wide 16:9 is no longer small. Marks, aspect guides and frame grabs follow.</li>
<li><b>Anamorphic desqueeze.</b> Color &#9656; Anamorphic Desqueeze (or right-click the picture): 1.25&#215; to 2&#215;, per clip, with Apply to All Clips. The picture, marks, guides, compare and frame grabs all use the desqueezed shape; Clip info shows both aspects. Movie exports are not desqueezed yet.</li>
<li><b>Compare pairs, finished.</b> A pair whose clips sit together moves as one block. Drag a clip onto the middle of another to pair them. <b>Auto-Pair Versions</b> pairs each shot&#8217;s newest version against the previous one. The side-by-side reel lays out each pair the way the pair is set.</li>
<li><b>Resume Hosting brings the web share back.</b> After a crash, reopening and resuming now restores the share itself, so browser guests keep seeing playlist changes, pairs and notes.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
